<title>UK: Coffee crop estimates - Main CENTAM plus MEXICO.</title>
<headline>Coffee crop estimates - Main CENTAM plus MEXICO.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following table gives latest estimates of 1996/97 coffee crops in main Central American coffee producing countries plus Mexico (estimates of 1995/96 crops in brackets).</p>
<p>Crop years and approximate main harvesting periods (as supplied by economists) follow each entry (in million 60 kg bags) -</p>
<p>SEE BELOW TABLE FOR MORE DETAILED NOTES ON HARVESTS, CRUCIAL WEATHER PERIODS.</p>
<p>							USDA	  FOLICHT</p>
<p>						     (DEC 13)    (DEC 20)</p>
<p> Costa Rica (Oct-Sep)			  2.5 (2.6)   2.28 (2.61)</p>
<p>(Sep-Feb)</p>
<p> El Salvador (Oct-Sep			  2.22 (2.33) 2.22 (2.33)</p>
<p>(Sep-Dec)</p>
<p> Guatemala (Oct-Sep)			   3.93 (3.83) 3.62 (3.61)</p>
<p>(Sep-Dec)</p>
<p> Honduras (Oct-Sep)			    2.5  (2.25) 2.21 (2.30)</p>
<p>(Oct-Jan)</p>
<p> Mexico  (Oct-Sep)			     5.4  (5.4)  5.15 (5.3)</p>
<p>(Aug-Nov and Nov-Jan)</p>
<p>NOTES -</p>
<p>MEXICO's harvest runs from late October to around late February. Harvesting starts in lower altitudes in Chiapas and around a month later it begins in more northerly states - Puebla and Veracruz. Harvesting ends in high altitudes in Chiapas in late January and the last beans from Veracruz are picked up to late February.</p>
